1
00:00:00,452 --> 00:00:03,495
(opening theme music)

2
00:00:05,788 --> 00:00:07,914
(singing in Japanese)

3
00:01:30,399 --> 00:01:31,191
Maki?

4
00:01:31,274 --> 00:01:33,984
The fact is, she's
a total weakling.

5
00:01:34,067 --> 00:01:36,359
She can't even see curses.

6
00:01:36,443 --> 00:01:39,360
She's just a normal person
swinging around cursed tools.

7
00:01:39,444 --> 00:01:41,569
She'll be a
fourth-grade forever.

8
00:01:41,652 --> 00:01:44,361
I don't know why she's
a jujutsu sorcerer at all.

9
00:01:44,445 --> 00:01:45,362
(Utahime claps)

10
00:01:45,446 --> 00:01:46,029
Okay break's over.

11
00:01:46,113 --> 00:01:47,946
(Mai sighs)

12
00:01:48,029 --> 00:01:49,030
[Miwa] I see!

13
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:51,781
Well, that's a relief!

14
00:01:53,073 --> 00:01:55,032
Stupid Mai! This
woman is no weakling!

15
00:01:57,992 --> 00:01:58,908
(Miwa yells)

16
00:01:58,992 --> 00:02:00,051
She's using a longer weapon,

17
00:02:00,075 --> 00:02:01,534
so I'd like to
close the distance,

18
00:02:01,617 --> 00:02:03,094
but all I can do is
dodge and parry her!

19
00:02:03,118 --> 00:02:05,410
If she were using the blade-

20
00:02:05,493 --> 00:02:06,577
(Miwa grunts)

21
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:07,661
I would've died twice!

22
00:02:08,286 --> 00:02:10,579
And she's only fourth-grade?

23
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:14,038
She could easily defeat
second-grade cursed spirits!

24
00:02:15,329 --> 00:02:16,372
(rock music)

25
00:02:16,456 --> 00:02:18,873
[Miwa] And how is she able
to swing such a long staff

26
00:02:18,956 --> 00:02:21,248
in this forest with so
much stuff in the way?

27
00:02:21,331 --> 00:02:23,083
(Miwa yells)

28
00:02:23,167 --> 00:02:26,750
(Miwa grunts)

29
00:02:26,834 --> 00:02:28,835
(water splashes)

30
00:02:28,918 --> 00:02:30,085
(Miwa pants)

31
00:02:30,169 --> 00:02:32,086
(Miwa sighs)

32
00:02:32,170 --> 00:02:36,045
(water splashes)

33
00:02:36,129 --> 00:02:38,463
(rock music)

34
00:02:41,297 --> 00:02:43,255
[Miwa] New Shadow Style,

35
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,965
Simple Domain!

36
00:02:47,757 --> 00:02:49,925
This allows me to attack
anything that enters

37
00:02:50,009 --> 00:02:53,093
the 2.21-meter radius of
my domain on full-auto reflex.

38
00:02:53,177 --> 00:02:55,426
It's released if my feet move

39
00:02:55,509 --> 00:02:57,094
from the point
were I activated it.

40
00:02:58,510 --> 00:03:00,595
Plus, my Quick
Draw is specialized

41
00:03:00,678 --> 00:03:01,928
against head-on attacks.

42
00:03:02,012 --> 00:03:04,679
It's the fastest technique
of the New Shadow School,

43
00:03:04,762 --> 00:03:06,305
wrapping my blade
in cursed energy

44
00:03:06,388 --> 00:03:08,264
while it's in the
sheath to accelerate it.

45
00:03:08,347 --> 00:03:10,473
But I don't think
this'll settle the match!

46
00:03:10,556 --> 00:03:13,141
I still have to create
an opening first!

47
00:03:13,224 --> 00:03:14,808
Iai-koh, huh?

48
00:03:14,892 --> 00:03:16,292
Looks like she has
some tricks, too.

49
00:03:16,349 --> 00:03:18,851
But there's a
difference in our reach.

50
00:03:18,934 --> 00:03:19,767
Rather than hit me,

51
00:03:19,851 --> 00:03:21,244
she wants to knock
away my cursed tool

52
00:03:21,268 --> 00:03:22,310
and create an opening.

53
00:03:23,186 --> 00:03:26,644
-So in that case-
-(weapon breaks)

54
00:03:26,729 --> 00:03:27,520
[Miwa] She broke it?

55
00:03:27,604 --> 00:03:29,062
She's giving up her
reach advantage?

56
00:03:29,146 --> 00:03:30,147
(weapon swings)

57
00:03:30,230 --> 00:03:31,147
[Miwa] She threw it!

58
00:03:31,230 --> 00:03:33,190
(Miwa grunts)

59
00:03:33,272 --> 00:03:35,522
A hidden weapon?

60
00:03:35,606 --> 00:03:37,374
She's trying to close
the gap by using a decoy!

61
00:03:37,398 --> 00:03:40,566
(Miwa grunts)

62
00:03:41,941 --> 00:03:43,234
My legs moved!

63
00:03:43,317 --> 00:03:44,400
But that's okay,

64
00:03:44,484 --> 00:03:46,128
I'll pull back and draw her
in close enough, and then-

65
00:03:46,152 --> 00:03:47,068
(Miwa grunts)

66
00:03:47,152 --> 00:03:50,236
(water splashes)

67
00:03:50,319 --> 00:03:53,320
[Miwa] Aikidou?
What a great move!

68
00:03:53,403 --> 00:03:55,071
Huh?

69
00:03:55,946 --> 00:03:57,572
Pretty nice sword you got here.

70
00:03:58,156 --> 00:04:00,531
Sword stealing?

71
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:01,199
Give it back?

72
00:04:01,281 --> 00:04:04,991
(music fades out)

73
00:04:05,949 --> 00:04:07,700
(Mei laughs)

74
00:04:07,783 --> 00:04:09,700
What an interesting girl.

75
00:04:09,784 --> 00:04:11,035
You should just go ahead

76
00:04:11,118 --> 00:04:12,178
and promote her to
second-grade already.

77
00:04:12,202 --> 00:04:15,368
Believe me, I feel the same way.

78
00:04:15,452 --> 00:04:17,912
But the Zen'in clan
keeps on interfering.

79
00:04:17,995 --> 00:04:20,954
I wish they would just change
their position and accept her.

80
00:04:21,829 --> 00:04:22,872
(Mei laughs)

81
00:04:22,955 --> 00:04:25,248
I can't understand such
restraint unless it's money.

82
00:04:25,331 --> 00:04:28,540
You're such a material girl.

83
00:04:28,624 --> 00:04:31,208
I'm more concerned about the
way the coverage around Yuuji

84
00:04:31,291 --> 00:04:32,917
keeps cutting out.

85
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,280
Animals can be fickle creatures.

86
00:04:34,334 --> 00:04:37,375
And sharing senses
with them is tiring.

87
00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:39,919
Yeah? I didn't know that.

88
00:04:40,002 --> 00:04:42,336
Which side're you
on anyway, Mei?

89
00:04:42,419 --> 00:04:43,587
Which side?

90
00:04:43,670 --> 00:04:45,587
I'm on the side of
money, of course.

91
00:04:45,670 --> 00:04:48,172
There's no value to anything
that can't be traded for money.

92
00:04:48,255 --> 00:04:50,964
If you can't make money
with it, what good is it?

93
00:04:51,048 --> 00:04:51,964
(Satoru laughs)

94
00:04:52,048 --> 00:04:54,216
[Satoru] Just how much
have you saved up?

95
00:04:55,507 --> 00:04:57,633
I don't know what
the old man's planning,

96
00:04:57,716 --> 00:04:59,235
but I do know he
won't find it that easy

97
00:04:59,259 --> 00:05:01,968
to deal with Yuuji anymore.

98
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:03,426
(charm catches on fire)

99
00:05:03,510 --> 00:05:04,968
Oh!

100
00:05:05,053 --> 00:05:06,094
They're on the move!

101
00:05:07,427 --> 00:05:08,637
(Curse 10A chitters)

102
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:10,386
The cursed spirits
released in the area

103
00:05:10,470 --> 00:05:12,096
all have charms on them.

104
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:15,430
-So when one disappears-
-(curse explodes)

105
00:05:15,514 --> 00:05:18,098
The corresponding charm
here in the viewing area

106
00:05:18,182 --> 00:05:19,182
is extinguished.

107
00:05:20,432 --> 00:05:22,641
Every charm is
extinguished differently

108
00:05:22,724 --> 00:05:24,850
according to the
registered cursed energy.

109
00:05:25,391 --> 00:05:28,185
When the Tokyo school
exorcises one, it burns red.

110
00:05:28,268 --> 00:05:32,978
When the Kyoto school
exorcises one, it burns blue.

111
00:05:33,062 --> 00:05:34,520
Since Maki is here,

112
00:05:34,603 --> 00:05:36,646
charms extinguished
by unregistered energy

113
00:05:36,729 --> 00:05:37,729
burn red as well.

114
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:40,855
Well, it's one to one.

115
00:05:40,939 --> 00:05:43,397
So how come no one's
paying attention to the game?

116
00:05:43,481 --> 00:05:45,541
Why can't both sides just
try being nice to each other?

117
00:05:45,565 --> 00:05:48,399
I guess they're all
too much like you.

118
00:05:48,483 --> 00:05:49,358
My only problem is you!

119
00:05:49,441 --> 00:05:51,400
[Kiyotaka] For the record,

120
00:05:51,484 --> 00:05:53,317
it was Panda who
took out Mechamaru.

121
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,401
Lucky!

122
00:05:55,318 --> 00:05:57,361
[Nobara] Come down
here, you goddamned witch!

123
00:05:57,444 --> 00:06:00,529
I've come down there
a few times already.

124
00:06:00,612 --> 00:06:03,320
Maybe you oughta
try and catch me!

125
00:06:03,403 --> 00:06:04,321
(intense music)

126
00:06:04,404 --> 00:06:05,321
[Momo] First-year!

127
00:06:05,404 --> 00:06:06,531
(ground explodes)

128
00:06:06,614 --> 00:06:07,656
(Nobara grunts)

129
00:06:07,739 --> 00:06:09,865
[Nobara] Her cursed energy
wind is like a hurricane!

130
00:06:09,949 --> 00:06:11,241
It's full of rocks and branches!

131
00:06:11,323 --> 00:06:13,491
If I drop my guard,
it'll rip my flesh!

132
00:06:16,159 --> 00:06:19,202
(Nobara gasps)

133
00:06:19,285 --> 00:06:21,785
(Nobara grunts)

134
00:06:23,036 --> 00:06:25,246
You dare damage
my precious face?

135
00:06:25,328 --> 00:06:27,411
A scar on the face is a
badge of honor for a man.

136
00:06:29,538 --> 00:06:32,289
Though it's just an
ugly flaw on a woman.

137
00:06:32,372 --> 00:06:34,081
Huh?

138
00:06:34,164 --> 00:06:36,540
You think jujutsu
sorcery is just strength.

139
00:06:36,623 --> 00:06:38,749
[Nobara] That's because it is.

140
00:06:38,832 --> 00:06:41,251
That's only true
for the men, though.

141
00:06:41,333 --> 00:06:41,833
[Nobara] What do you mean?

142
00:06:41,917 --> 00:06:43,918
Even if they're strong,

143
00:06:44,001 --> 00:06:46,877
women have to be cute,
too, or they'll be undervalued.

144
00:06:46,961 --> 00:06:48,460
And of course,
even if they're cute,

145
00:06:48,544 --> 00:06:50,087
they'll still be undervalued,

146
00:06:50,170 --> 00:06:52,212
unless they're also strong.

147
00:06:52,295 --> 00:06:53,296
Do you get it?

148
00:06:54,504 --> 00:06:56,481
They don't demand strength
from female jujutsu sorcerers.

149
00:06:56,505 --> 00:06:59,257
They demand perfection!

150
00:07:00,881 --> 00:07:01,798
And what's worse?

151
00:07:01,882 --> 00:07:03,423
Mai has to fight against demands

152
00:07:03,507 --> 00:07:05,466
that're even more outrageous!

153
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:08,342
One thing that I do
get is that you are

154
00:07:08,425 --> 00:07:10,676
a pain in the ass!

155
00:07:10,759 --> 00:07:12,969
(Momo slides)

156
00:07:13,052 --> 00:07:14,469
(wind whips)

157
00:07:17,053 --> 00:07:17,929
[Momo] She's only a first-year

158
00:07:18,012 --> 00:07:20,638
and she's already this
accustomed to fighting?

159
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:22,972
She's still going strong

160
00:07:23,055 --> 00:07:25,014
no matter how
many times I blast her.

161
00:07:25,889 --> 00:07:26,890
That was nothing.

162
00:07:28,099 --> 00:07:30,016
I'm used to getting
knocked around.

163
00:07:30,683 --> 00:07:34,350
[Momo] If I up my output
any further, I might kill her.

164
00:07:34,892 --> 00:07:36,977
No, that's just an excuse.

165
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:40,019
The real reason I can't
attack her is Inumaki.

166
00:07:41,394 --> 00:07:42,395
(camera shutters)

167
00:07:42,478 --> 00:07:44,187
What is cursed speech?

168
00:07:44,271 --> 00:07:46,563
It just uses the power of words.

169
00:07:46,646 --> 00:07:48,480
It imbues cursed
energy into sound,

170
00:07:48,564 --> 00:07:51,315
so all you have to do
is to protect your brain

171
00:07:51,398 --> 00:07:52,541
and your ears
with cursed energy.

172
00:07:52,565 --> 00:07:55,482
Cursed speech is a
technique specialized

173
00:07:55,566 --> 00:07:56,750
for use against cursed spirits,

174
00:07:56,774 --> 00:07:59,400
and it's nothing to be afraid
of if you know it's coming.

175
00:07:59,483 --> 00:08:01,693
[Momo] Yes, but
if you don't know

176
00:08:01,776 --> 00:08:03,319
whether it's coming or not,

177
00:08:03,402 --> 00:08:05,027
then you're
constantly distracted!

178
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:07,712
And I'm not used to
protecting the inside of my head

179
00:08:07,736 --> 00:08:09,529
in the first place!

180
00:08:09,612 --> 00:08:12,697
He's such a nuisance,
whether he's here or not!

181
00:08:13,572 --> 00:08:15,030
Done lecturing?

182
00:08:15,114 --> 00:08:16,240
About time!

183
00:08:17,282 --> 00:08:19,615
Even perfection is easy,

184
00:08:19,699 --> 00:08:21,699
compared to what's always
been demanded of Mai!

185
00:08:21,783 --> 00:08:23,700
She's from one of
the three major clans

186
00:08:23,783 --> 00:08:25,701
of elite jujutsu sorcerers!

187
00:08:25,784 --> 00:08:28,077
The Zen'in Clan!

188
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:30,286
Where perfection's
expected, and demanded.

189
00:08:31,369 --> 00:08:35,079
They say, "Inherit the Zen'in
clan's hereditary technique!"

190
00:08:35,162 --> 00:08:36,745
And any who don't
meet that demand

191
00:08:36,829 --> 00:08:39,122
start their sorcerer
lives as failures.

192
00:08:39,830 --> 00:08:40,914
What's even worse,

193
00:08:40,998 --> 00:08:44,456
women aren't even allowed
to stand at the starting line.

194
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:46,457
Without the Zen'in clan lineage,

195
00:08:46,541 --> 00:08:49,667
they're not considered
to be real jujutsu sorcerers.

196
00:08:50,458 --> 00:08:54,085
And, if they're not considered
to be jujutsu sorcerers,

197
00:08:54,168 --> 00:08:55,919
they're not even
recognized as people!

198
00:08:56,669 --> 00:08:59,920
She's lived her
entire life scorned

199
00:09:00,004 --> 00:09:02,421
in a family without
a shred of affection.

200
00:09:02,504 --> 00:09:03,647
The suffering Mai went through

201
00:09:03,671 --> 00:09:06,380
to experience what
we all take for granted.

202
00:09:07,006 --> 00:09:08,506
Why don't you try
thinking that over

203
00:09:08,590 --> 00:09:10,923
with that confused
brain of yours?

204
00:09:11,882 --> 00:09:12,757
You have a curse for a friend!

205
00:09:12,841 --> 00:09:14,508
(Momo yells)

206
00:09:16,050 --> 00:09:17,135
Shut up.

207
00:09:17,218 --> 00:09:20,010
You think misfortune is a
free pass to do anything?

208
00:09:21,677 --> 00:09:22,760
What, then?

209
00:09:22,844 --> 00:09:23,678
You're okay with
those who are blessed

210
00:09:23,761 --> 00:09:25,636
getting trash-talked
behind their backs?

211
00:09:26,721 --> 00:09:28,971
That's just like Saori!

212
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:33,431
I can't stand her!
Regardless of her upbringing!

213
00:09:34,848 --> 00:09:39,017
And I love Maki, who had to
endure the same upbringing!

214
00:09:40,058 --> 00:09:42,184
Have any of you even
bothered to think about

215
00:09:42,268 --> 00:09:44,559
what kind of person the
idiot you're trying to curse is?

216
00:09:44,642 --> 00:09:48,353
What makes you think
any one of us is obligated

217
00:09:48,436 --> 00:09:51,979
to attain perfection, or
such absurd demands?

218
00:09:53,104 --> 00:09:56,355
Is your entire life just a job?

219
00:09:56,438 --> 00:09:57,647
Straw doll-

220
00:09:57,731 --> 00:09:58,564
Hairpin Technique!

221
00:09:58,647 --> 00:10:01,982
(trees shake)

222
00:10:04,733 --> 00:10:07,192
[Momo] This must be why
she kept shooting those nails

223
00:10:07,276 --> 00:10:08,734
that didn't land any hits!

224
00:10:08,817 --> 00:10:11,651
(electronic music)

225
00:10:13,111 --> 00:10:14,652
(Momo grunts)

226
00:10:17,279 --> 00:10:18,613
(Momo sighs)

227
00:10:20,738 --> 00:10:24,197
(Nobara grunts)

228
00:10:24,906 --> 00:10:27,615
You came close, but you
still couldn't reach me!

229
00:10:27,698 --> 00:10:31,284
(Nobara falls)

230
00:10:31,367 --> 00:10:32,284
Wrong!

231
00:10:32,367 --> 00:10:33,367
I reached you, alright!

232
00:10:34,618 --> 00:10:36,035
This is plenty!

233
00:10:36,784 --> 00:10:38,244
[Momo] A bristle from my broom?

234
00:10:38,328 --> 00:10:39,702
She pulled it out just now!

235
00:10:39,785 --> 00:10:42,245
I don't give a damn
about your "men are this"

236
00:10:42,329 --> 00:10:43,912
and "women have to be that!"

237
00:10:43,996 --> 00:10:45,871
You can keep all
that shit to yourself!

238
00:10:47,122 --> 00:10:49,042
I love myself when I'm
pretty and all dressed up!

239
00:10:50,332 --> 00:10:53,582
And I love myself
when I'm kicking ass!

240
00:10:53,665 --> 00:10:55,333
(Nobara grunts)

241
00:10:55,415 --> 00:10:55,916
(hammer strikes)

242
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,709
I am Nobara Kugisaki!

243
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:01,793
(Momo grunts)

244
00:11:01,877 --> 00:11:03,020
[Momo] I can't control my broom!

245
00:11:03,044 --> 00:11:06,711
[Nobara] If I hit her with
my hammer, I might kill her!

246
00:11:06,794 --> 00:11:08,462
(Momo grunts)

247
00:11:08,545 --> 00:11:10,921
-[Nobara] So- -(Momo gasps)

248
00:11:11,005 --> 00:11:12,755
[Momo] A squeaky hammer?

249
00:11:12,838 --> 00:11:14,839
(Nobara yells)

250
00:11:14,922 --> 00:11:16,464
(Momo shrieks)

251
00:11:16,547 --> 00:11:18,882
(Momo grunts)

252
00:11:20,383 --> 00:11:21,924
(Momo sighs)

253
00:11:22,008 --> 00:11:24,467
Now, one more time!

254
00:11:24,550 --> 00:11:26,885
(bullet strikes)

255
00:11:26,968 --> 00:11:28,509
(Momo gasps)

256
00:11:28,593 --> 00:11:31,469
(wind swooshes)

257
00:11:31,552 --> 00:11:33,511
Just barely within
effective range.

258
00:11:34,428 --> 00:11:36,138
And just in time.

259
00:11:36,221 --> 00:11:38,138
One hell of a shot.

260
00:11:38,221 --> 00:11:40,680
(intense music)

261
00:11:43,681 --> 00:11:46,183
(intense music)

262
00:11:49,225 --> 00:11:50,516
Hello, Momo?

263
00:11:51,268 --> 00:11:54,019
Don't worry, it
was a rubber bullet.

264
00:11:54,102 --> 00:11:56,144
More important,
wasn't that bright light

265
00:11:56,227 --> 00:11:58,519
Mechamaru's Ultimate Cannon?

266
00:11:58,603 --> 00:12:01,646
And now all of a sudden
I can't get a hold of him.

267
00:12:01,729 --> 00:12:04,397
If he felt cornered enough to
use such a powerful technique,

268
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:05,813
and now he's missing,

269
00:12:05,897 --> 00:12:08,689
then he probably lost
and Panda's still around.

270
00:12:08,773 --> 00:12:09,523
You should get outta there

271
00:12:09,607 --> 00:12:10,916
and go back to
patrolling from the air.

272
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:12,775
Without you,
we're all in trouble.

273
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:14,900
Mm.

274
00:12:16,484 --> 00:12:17,567
Hey,

275
00:12:17,651 --> 00:12:18,652
Mai, I, uh-

276
00:12:19,485 --> 00:12:22,527
It's okay, Momo. I understand.

277
00:12:22,611 --> 00:12:23,611
[Momo] Thanks.

278
00:12:24,444 --> 00:12:25,528
What's this?

279
00:12:25,612 --> 00:12:27,821
Aren't you going
to call your friends?

280
00:12:27,905 --> 00:12:29,655
Well, it's fine by me.

281
00:12:29,738 --> 00:12:32,406
I can still take you,
even two-on-one.

282
00:12:32,489 --> 00:12:35,448
There are lots of different
ways to enjoy this, right?

283
00:12:35,948 --> 00:12:38,783
Sure, I could have
everyone beat you together.

284
00:12:38,866 --> 00:12:40,227
But I'm going to
enjoy beating you,

285
00:12:41,117 --> 00:12:43,410
by myself.

286
00:12:43,493 --> 00:12:45,701
You ought to call me "Big Sis,"

287
00:12:45,785 --> 00:12:46,786
little sister.

288
00:12:48,328 --> 00:12:49,787
So, hey. How do
you feel about Maki?

289
00:12:49,870 --> 00:12:54,413
Aaagh, she's gonna hate
it no matter what I say!

290
00:12:54,496 --> 00:12:57,580
Uh, I think she's a smart
and wonderful woman.

291
00:12:57,664 --> 00:12:58,581
Huh?

292
00:12:58,665 --> 00:13:00,082
I'm talking about as a sorcerer.

293
00:13:00,165 --> 00:13:02,874
Oh, really? What a relief!

294
00:13:05,042 --> 00:13:06,250
To be honest,

295
00:13:06,334 --> 00:13:09,251
I still don't know all
that much about jujutsu.

296
00:13:09,335 --> 00:13:10,919
But Maki's really
strong in a fight.

297
00:13:11,002 --> 00:13:13,127
Maybe it's her balance?

298
00:13:13,211 --> 00:13:15,087
Even just the way
she walks is scary!

299
00:13:15,170 --> 00:13:16,836
Don't forget. She's
a fourth-grade.

300
00:13:17,504 --> 00:13:18,962
Huh? Really?

301
00:13:19,046 --> 00:13:22,089
She's from a famous
sorcerer clan family.

302
00:13:23,589 --> 00:13:25,756
But she left them and
so they've been interfering

303
00:13:25,839 --> 00:13:27,882
with her promotion
ever since she left.

304
00:13:28,924 --> 00:13:30,633
Why's a sorcerer family

305
00:13:30,716 --> 00:13:33,301
not accepting of
a sorcerer like her?

306
00:13:33,385 --> 00:13:36,260
They refuse to acknowledge
what they've already rejected

307
00:13:36,344 --> 00:13:38,010
because they're idiots.

308
00:13:38,094 --> 00:13:39,844
Still, if she does
well in the Event,

309
00:13:39,928 --> 00:13:43,512
and Maki's name starts
to become better known,

310
00:13:43,595 --> 00:13:45,971
it's going to be harder for
them to harass her like that.

311
00:13:46,055 --> 00:13:50,014
So let's start by winning
the group battle, you guys!

312
00:13:50,098 --> 00:13:53,140
You have to fight like you're
about to die all over again!

313
00:13:53,224 --> 00:13:54,141
Right.

314
00:13:54,225 --> 00:13:55,683
[Maki] I can hear you, you know.

315
00:13:55,766 --> 00:13:57,351
(Yuuji, Nobara, and Panda gasp)

316
00:13:57,434 --> 00:13:58,434
Jeez.

317
00:13:59,059 --> 00:14:01,060
I should know better

318
00:14:01,143 --> 00:14:03,353
than to let myself
get distracted like that.

319
00:14:03,436 --> 00:14:04,560
(gun clanks)

320
00:14:04,644 --> 00:14:06,062
What're you smiling about?

321
00:14:06,145 --> 00:14:08,187
(gun shoots)

322
00:14:08,270 --> 00:14:08,895
(bullet slices)

323
00:14:08,978 --> 00:14:11,938
(branches swinging)

324
00:14:13,106 --> 00:14:14,022
(gun shoots)

325
00:14:14,106 --> 00:14:15,940
So what if she
hides out of sight?

326
00:14:18,148 --> 00:14:19,209
Are you just trying
to gain distance?

327
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:21,191
Well, that won't work!

328
00:14:21,274 --> 00:14:22,692
-(sword swings)
-(tree breaks)

329
00:14:22,775 --> 00:14:23,817
[Mai] Shit!

330
00:14:25,151 --> 00:14:27,360
(gun shoots)

331
00:14:27,443 --> 00:14:28,027
(Mai grunts)

332
00:14:28,111 --> 00:14:30,361
[Mai] From below?

333
00:14:30,444 --> 00:14:31,362
I should've known!

334
00:14:31,445 --> 00:14:33,195
Maki has a talent I don't.

335
00:14:34,071 --> 00:14:38,114
So, have you heard?
About Ougi's daughters?

336
00:14:38,197 --> 00:14:39,948
One of them can't
even see curses,

337
00:14:40,031 --> 00:14:41,572
much less use techniques.

338
00:14:41,656 --> 00:14:44,573
Twins are always
a sign of ill fortune.

339
00:14:44,657 --> 00:14:46,259
[Clan Elder] Thank heaven
they're daughters, at least.

340
00:14:46,283 --> 00:14:50,575
I couldn't bear to see an
eldest son as a lowly servant.

341
00:14:51,659 --> 00:14:54,035
(somber music)

342
00:14:55,494 --> 00:14:57,078
Mai? What's the matter with you?

343
00:14:57,161 --> 00:14:59,246
Let's go! Hurry up!

344
00:15:01,663 --> 00:15:02,122
I'm afraid.

345
00:15:02,205 --> 00:15:04,247
[Maki] Afraid of what?

346
00:15:04,330 --> 00:15:06,331
Come on, if we're late
again, we'll get in trouble.

347
00:15:08,498 --> 00:15:09,498
It's them.

348
00:15:12,833 --> 00:15:14,000
Again?

349
00:15:14,084 --> 00:15:15,959
(Maki sighs)

350
00:15:16,042 --> 00:15:18,127
All right, I'll help you out.

351
00:15:18,210 --> 00:15:19,210
Are you ho-o-

352
00:15:21,794 --> 00:15:24,421
[Maki] Come on,
just close your eyes.

353
00:15:24,503 --> 00:15:27,004
(curse warbles)

354
00:15:28,713 --> 00:15:31,630
If you can't see them, it's
like they're not even there.

355
00:15:31,714 --> 00:15:33,465
(Mai whimpers)

356
00:15:33,548 --> 00:15:36,007
[Mai] You always acted
like you had no fear,

357
00:15:37,383 --> 00:15:40,467
and plowed forward
toward your future!

358
00:15:40,550 --> 00:15:43,176
I always hated you for that.

359
00:15:43,260 --> 00:15:44,260
(somber music)

360
00:15:44,343 --> 00:15:47,010
So you're leaving
the clan, Maki?

361
00:15:47,094 --> 00:15:49,053
You seem to have
plenty of servants around.

362
00:15:49,137 --> 00:15:51,637
I doubt you'll miss me at all.

363
00:15:51,721 --> 00:15:54,930
But I do intend to return
someday, Clan Leader.

364
00:15:55,013 --> 00:15:55,930
(Naobito gulps)

365
00:15:56,013 --> 00:15:56,931
(Naobito exhales)

366
00:15:57,014 --> 00:15:58,931
Why would you return?

367
00:15:59,014 --> 00:16:02,141
So I can become the
head of the Zen'in Clan!

368
00:16:02,224 --> 00:16:05,516
(Naobito laughs)

369
00:16:05,599 --> 00:16:06,726
Well, if that's the case,

370
00:16:06,809 --> 00:16:09,977
I'll put you through ordeals
you'll be lucky to survive!

371
00:16:10,060 --> 00:16:11,477
(somber music)

372
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:12,561
You can do as you please.

373
00:16:13,186 --> 00:16:15,479
[Naobito] And Mai, as well.

374
00:16:18,813 --> 00:16:20,313
Mai's not involved in this.

375
00:16:21,398 --> 00:16:23,981
(somber music)

376
00:16:29,233 --> 00:16:31,109
What a liar.

377
00:16:32,317 --> 00:16:33,317
(sword clangs)

378
00:16:33,401 --> 00:16:35,776
[Mai] I hate you!

379
00:16:37,610 --> 00:16:38,319
(gun shoots)

380
00:16:38,403 --> 00:16:41,737
(bullets fall)

381
00:16:41,820 --> 00:16:43,321
(gun reloads)

382
00:16:43,405 --> 00:16:44,529
(Mai inhales)

383
00:16:44,612 --> 00:16:47,780
(Mai exhales)

384
00:16:47,864 --> 00:16:50,407
(Maki sighs)

385
00:16:50,490 --> 00:16:52,741
(gun shoots)

386
00:16:52,824 --> 00:16:55,783
(footsteps running)

387
00:16:56,992 --> 00:16:59,201
(gun shoots)

388
00:17:01,994 --> 00:17:04,202
(gun shoots)

389
00:17:05,995 --> 00:17:07,787
(gun shoots)

390
00:17:07,871 --> 00:17:11,580
(footsteps running)

391
00:17:11,663 --> 00:17:14,581
(out-of-tune music)

392
00:17:20,333 --> 00:17:21,250
(gun shoots)

393
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:24,334
(sword slashes) [Maki]
That was your sixth shot!

394
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:25,960
I won't let you reload!

395
00:17:26,043 --> 00:17:27,043
[Mai] I hate you.

396
00:17:28,335 --> 00:17:29,253
(gun shoots)

397
00:17:29,336 --> 00:17:30,336
[Mai] I hate you.

398
00:17:31,503 --> 00:17:33,463
I hate you!

399
00:17:35,297 --> 00:17:37,629
Which is why

400
00:17:37,713 --> 00:17:38,881
I never told you

401
00:17:39,256 --> 00:17:41,173
about my first love,

402
00:17:41,257 --> 00:17:43,673
or about my technique!

403
00:17:44,924 --> 00:17:47,300
[Utahime] "Construction"
uses one's cursed energy

404
00:17:47,384 --> 00:17:50,843
to create matter from nothing.

405
00:17:50,926 --> 00:17:52,885
It differs from
the manifestation

406
00:17:52,968 --> 00:17:53,844
of an innate domain

407
00:17:53,927 --> 00:17:56,970
within the barrier of
a domain expansion.

408
00:17:57,053 --> 00:17:58,280
The matter produced
by Construction

409
00:17:58,304 --> 00:18:02,013
doesn't disappear when
the cursed technique ends.

410
00:18:03,264 --> 00:18:05,473
Because of that, it consumes
a lot of cursed energy,

411
00:18:05,555 --> 00:18:08,223
and puts a heavy
strain on the body.

412
00:18:09,475 --> 00:18:12,225
Creating one bullet a
day, is Mai's maximum.

413
00:18:12,558 --> 00:18:15,018
So she uses a revolver

414
00:18:15,101 --> 00:18:18,102
to create confusion about
how many bullets she has left.

415
00:18:19,935 --> 00:18:20,311
[Mai] I win.

416
00:18:20,394 --> 00:18:21,561
I win!

417
00:18:24,771 --> 00:18:26,354
(Maki grunts)

418
00:18:28,730 --> 00:18:29,646
[Mai] She-

419
00:18:29,730 --> 00:18:31,731
She caught the bullet?

420
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:34,357
(Maki grunts)

421
00:18:34,441 --> 00:18:37,317
I should never do that
with my bare hands.

422
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,859
(Mai gasps)

423
00:18:39,942 --> 00:18:41,650
(Mai grunts)

424
00:18:41,734 --> 00:18:42,735
(Mai yells)

425
00:18:42,777 --> 00:18:45,444
[Mai] Maki has a talent I don't.

426
00:18:45,527 --> 00:18:46,903
(Mai grunts)

427
00:18:46,986 --> 00:18:49,737
[Mai] Like Mechamaru,
she has a Heavenly Pact,

428
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:51,029
but hers is somehow different.

429
00:18:51,112 --> 00:18:53,738
Normally, she would have been
born with a cursed technique.

430
00:18:53,821 --> 00:18:55,072
(Maki grunts)

431
00:18:55,156 --> 00:18:56,072
(Mai grunts)

432
00:18:56,156 --> 00:18:57,396
[Mai] But in exchange for that,

433
00:18:57,448 --> 00:18:59,324
she was granted
superhuman physical abilities.

434
00:19:01,032 --> 00:19:02,283
(Mai sighs)

435
00:19:02,366 --> 00:19:03,592
[Mai] The Zen'in clan
would never acknowledge it.

436
00:19:03,616 --> 00:19:06,201
That this was a talent.

437
00:19:06,284 --> 00:19:07,201
(Mai grunts)

438
00:19:07,285 --> 00:19:08,285
[Mai] That I lacked!

439
00:19:09,452 --> 00:19:11,911
Well, what now?

440
00:19:11,994 --> 00:19:13,745
Is this settled, then?

441
00:19:13,828 --> 00:19:15,412
Why?

442
00:19:15,496 --> 00:19:18,704
Why did you leave the clan?

443
00:19:18,788 --> 00:19:21,372
Come on! You know
the answer to that!

444
00:19:21,456 --> 00:19:23,165
You joined Jujutsu High, too!

445
00:19:23,248 --> 00:19:24,457
Wrong!

446
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:25,457
-(Maki gasps)
-(Mai sobs)

447
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:27,582
I never wanted to
be a jujutsu sorcerer!

448
00:19:27,665 --> 00:19:30,250
It's all your fault!

449
00:19:30,334 --> 00:19:32,168
Because you tried
so hard to be one,

450
00:19:32,251 --> 00:19:34,584
I was forced to follow
in your footsteps!

451
00:19:35,877 --> 00:19:39,586
I'm so sick of facing
all these scary things!

452
00:19:39,669 --> 00:19:42,338
What was so awful about being
ordered around back home?

453
00:19:42,421 --> 00:19:45,255
We could have just
done a few chores,

454
00:19:45,339 --> 00:19:47,507
and lived like
everyone else does!

455
00:19:47,589 --> 00:19:50,590
(Mai sobs)

456
00:19:50,673 --> 00:19:52,341
Why couldn't you have

457
00:19:52,424 --> 00:19:56,050
just stayed and been satisfied
down at the bottom with me?

458
00:19:57,051 --> 00:19:58,634
(sad music)

459
00:20:01,843 --> 00:20:02,844
Because,

460
00:20:04,011 --> 00:20:05,772
I would have hated
myself if I had done that.

461
00:20:07,513 --> 00:20:08,513
That's why.

462
00:20:10,721 --> 00:20:11,847
I'm sorry.

463
00:20:11,931 --> 00:20:13,639
(Mai sobs)

464
00:20:13,722 --> 00:20:15,848
(sad music)

465
00:20:15,932 --> 00:20:18,475
[Mai] Big sister! Don't let go!

466
00:20:18,558 --> 00:20:21,016
[Maki] I won't let go.

467
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:22,184
[Mai] You never will?

468
00:20:22,267 --> 00:20:24,017
[Maki] Jeez, give it a rest.

469
00:20:24,101 --> 00:20:26,393
[Mai] Never leave me behind.

470
00:20:26,477 --> 00:20:27,811
[Maki] Of course I won't.

471
00:20:30,102 --> 00:20:32,479
After all, we're sisters.

472
00:20:32,562 --> 00:20:35,896
(piano music)

473
00:20:35,979 --> 00:20:37,814
[Mai] What a liar.

474
00:20:39,606 --> 00:20:40,856
I hate you.

475
00:20:45,775 --> 00:20:48,692
(closing theme music)

476
00:20:55,820 --> 00:20:58,946
(singing in Japanese)

477
00:22:15,929 --> 00:22:17,679
[Miwa, Momo,
and Mai] Juju Stroll!

478
00:22:17,762 --> 00:22:21,014
(bored music)

479
00:22:25,474 --> 00:22:26,849
[Miwa] I'm so hungry.

480
00:22:28,433 --> 00:22:30,601
Fortunately, I think my left
over edamame from lunch

481
00:22:30,684 --> 00:22:33,352
is still in the fridge.

482
00:22:33,435 --> 00:22:35,477
(Momo and Mai chewing)

483
00:22:35,561 --> 00:22:36,562
-Hm?
-Hm?

484
00:22:38,103 --> 00:22:39,604
(Miwa grunts)

485
00:22:41,479 --> 00:22:44,230
(Momo chewing)

486
00:22:44,313 --> 00:22:45,647
(Momo swallows)

487
00:22:45,730 --> 00:22:47,022
Sorry.

488
00:22:47,106 --> 00:22:49,648
[Miwa] You could at least
try to look a little guilty!

489
00:22:50,940 --> 00:22:53,983
[Momo] As a token of
my apology, have this.

490
00:22:54,066 --> 00:22:54,691
(Miwa sighs) No,
I'm not interested

491
00:22:54,775 --> 00:22:57,234
in late-night cup ramen.

492
00:22:57,317 --> 00:22:59,901
(Momo laughs)

493
00:22:59,985 --> 00:23:01,236
How about this?

494
00:23:01,319 --> 00:23:03,528
Nishimiya-style
Seafood Cup Ramen!

495
00:23:04,987 --> 00:23:08,029
Step one, use scissors to
chop up hot chili peppers

496
00:23:08,113 --> 00:23:10,239
into the seafood cup ramen!

497
00:23:10,322 --> 00:23:12,905
Two: Fill the container
halfway with milk.

498
00:23:12,989 --> 00:23:16,699
Three: Add hot water
up to the line inside!

499
00:23:16,782 --> 00:23:19,062
Since we're using milk, make
sure the water's boiling hot!

500
00:23:23,326 --> 00:23:24,701
(Miwa slurps)

501
00:23:24,784 --> 00:23:27,077
(Miwa gasps)

502
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:29,287
[Miwa] This is good!
It's really good!

503
00:23:29,370 --> 00:23:30,287
[Momo] Right?

504
00:23:30,370 --> 00:23:31,805
[Mai] Maybe I'll
have it next time, too.

505
00:23:31,829 --> 00:23:34,246
Why didn't you eat this?

506
00:23:34,329 --> 00:23:35,622
Instead of taking my edamame.

507
00:23:35,705 --> 00:23:38,331
(Miwa slurps)

508
00:23:38,415 --> 00:23:40,331
Well, you still pay the price

509
00:23:40,415 --> 00:23:42,332
for late-night cup
ramen the next day.

510
00:23:42,416 --> 00:23:43,416
Mm-hm, mm-hm.

511
00:23:45,375 --> 00:23:48,376
(intense rock music)

